.TH "CSDLC-GITHUB" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-github \- retired generic mutation writer; use issue\-scoped GitHub intents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc github\-issue ISSUE \-\-operation OPERATION.json [\-\-execute]
\&csdlc github\-pr ISSUE \-\-operation OPERATION.json [\-\-execute]
\&csdlc github \-\-help
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&The generic github \-\-request writer is retired and fails before request parsing or transport. Use the issue\-scoped github\-issue or github\-pr semantic intent. The github command remains discoverable through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration.
.SH OPTIONS
\&\-\-operation: Reviewed issue or pull\-request operation content for the semantic owner.
.PP
\&\-\-execute: Execute an admitted github\-issue or github\-pr operation.
.PP
\&\-\-request and \-\-observe\-github: Retired generic\-writer inputs documented only for migration discovery.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show migration guidance; \-h is equivalent.
.SH REQUEST
\&Use the issue\-scoped semantic operation or an exact generated \-\-intent\-request. OperationalRemoteDispatchRequest is a retired direct\-writer input.
.SH EFFECTS
\&Discovery is read\-only. Remote effects belong to github\-issue and github\-pr semantic transactions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&csdlc github\-issue 870 \-\-operation issue\-operation.json \-\-execute
.fi
.SH RECOVERY
\&After uncertain dispatch retain the original request and exact intent. Reinvoke the identical native request for authenticated reconciliation. A changed request is a different operation, not a retry. Never delete the target guard or intent to force a second write.
.PP
\&Issue\-edit does not support write replay, including retry_after_authenticated_absence; reconcile exact retained target and preserve later human changes. Supported create/ready absence retry is explicit, authenticated and one\-shot. Merge retries are always read\-only; a still\-open or uncertain PR remains blocked.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1), csdlc\-finish(1).
